     "text": "{\"count\": 2, \"rationale\": \"The target crown:obtain is reached through h4_0:obtain or h4_1:pivot. Those two steps are fed by three steps: h3_1:pivot, h2_0:traverse and h3_2:obtain. h3_1 and h2_0 both depend only on h1_1:escalate, an AND step whose parents are the two footholds. h3_2:obtain is reached from h1_0:obtain or h1_2:escalate. Blocking h1_1:escalate and h3_2:obtain therefore cuts every path to the target; blocking h4_0 and h4_1 would also work. No single block is enough. Blocking h1_1 leaves the path through h3_2 to h4_1, and blocking h3_2 leaves the path through h1_1 and h2_0 to h4_0. Blocking only h4_0 or only h4_1 leaves the other one open. The minimum is 2.\"}"
